### Atlas S14 — reporting read models, N+1-free, by hand.
### Set @token from a register-org / login response (an OrgAdmin or HrManager).
### Seed some data first: hire a few workers in different countries, record a soon-expiring
### document or two, and execute a payroll run — then the reports below have something to show.

@base = http://localhost:5080/api/v1
@token = PASTE_A_SESSION_TOKEN

### Headcount by country, in-probation split as of today (pin ?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD to ask about a past day).
GET {{base}}/reports/headcount
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Headcount as of a chosen date — "who was in probation on this day?"
GET {{base}}/reports/headcount?asOf=2026-06-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Employment cost for a month, grouped by country + currency — folded from EXECUTED runs only.
### Defaults to the current month when year/month are omitted.
GET {{base}}/reports/employment-cost?year=2026&month=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An impossible month is a 400 (parse-and-reject, not an empty report hiding a typo).
GET {{base}}/reports/employment-cost?year=2026&month=13
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Upcoming renewals/expiries in the next 90 days (JSON). Pin ?withinDays= to widen or narrow.
GET {{base}}/reports/renewals?withinDays=90
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The SAME query as a streaming CSV export — memory-bounded, rows written as they arrive.
### Authorization + validation happen BEFORE the first byte; once streaming starts the status is 200.
GET {{base}}/reports/renewals.csv?withinDays=90
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The org compliance roster — every active worker with a compliant/non-compliant verdict.
### This is the N+1 hunt's payoff: it answers across the whole org in a fixed 2 queries, not 1+N.
### Non-compliant workers sort first (the worklist a compliance officer acts on).
GET {{base}}/reports/compliance-roster
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reference data — the supported countries. Cached (ledger entry #1); safe because it is the same
### for every org and changes only on deploy. Never do this for per-org data.
GET {{base}}/reports/meta/countries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Anonymous is a 401 — reports name people and pay; the whole surface is behind a token.
GET {{base}}/reports/headcount

